A split composition in the style of Piet Mondrian: bold black grid lines dividing the canvas into geometric rectangles filled with primary colors—red, yellow, blue, and white. On one side, abstracted forms suggesting laboratory vessels and molecular structures rendered in clean blue and white blocks. On the other side, earthy brown and golden yellow rectangles arranged to evoke industrial pipes and flowing channels, with small gold squares scattered throughout suggesting wealth. The two halves connected by the rigid black grid, creating visual tension between the sections while maintaining perfect geometric balance. The composition asks a silent question through its stark division and contrasting color temperatures.
